  "findings": [
    "DFG operation-node ratio is not tensor FLOPs per byte; shared-buffer and reduction dependencies still matter.",
    "RTL/45 nm synthesis and Timeloop end-to-end modeling; U280 DMA measurement is one component, not fabricated PICACHU system timing.",
    "A100 comparison scales the systolic array and CGRA; GEMM and nonlinear paths both change, so total speedup is not an isolated nonlinear-unit effect.",
    "Figure 7c shows the finite buffers below unlimited; prose about no additional gain above 40KB is insufficient to prove a universal capacity threshold.",
    "Table 1 displays tanh with numerator and denominator reversed; preserve original and do not copy as an executable formula. Fixed-position RoPE is linear in Q/K and cached coefficients can change actual operator demand."
